WEBVTT

00:00:00.466 --> 00:00:06.868
Your notes are everywhere. With Révise, all your revision finally lives in one place.

00:00:08.566 --> 00:00:13.440
First, tell Révise how you like to learn, and its explanations adapt to you.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:22.211
Drop in your PDFs, Word documents, Excel sheets, and even past exam papers. Everything stays on your computer.

00:00:23.266 --> 00:00:28.351
Révise splits your course into chapters, and tracks what you have really mastered in each one.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:35.410
In one click, your revision sheet is ready, with definitions, formulas, and common traps.

00:00:36.466 --> 00:00:43.077
Every sentence links to the exact page of your course. One click, and you can check it. Nothing is made up.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:47.974
Stuck on an idea? Ask for it explained as if you were twelve.

00:00:49.666 --> 00:00:56.966
Your flashcards come back right when you were about to forget them. That's spaced repetition, the most effective way to memorize.

00:00:58.766 --> 00:01:05.542
Practice with quizzes at the difficulty you choose. Every mistake is explained, then turned into a flashcard.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:14.192
Sit timed mock exams in real conditions. The AI grades you with a realistic marking scheme, and explains what went wrong.

00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:19.592
Révise analyzes past papers to find the chapters that come up most often.

00:01:20.633 --> 00:01:26.120
Ask your course anything. Answers rely on your own documents, and always cite the page.

00:01:27.166 --> 00:01:33.802
A mind map puts the whole subject on one page. Click a notion, and its course passage opens right beside it.

00:01:34.866 --> 00:01:46.008
To revise on the go, Révise turns your chapters into a podcast: two hosts talk it through, with the source under every line. Your NotebookLM overviews fit right in too.

00:01:47.066 --> 00:01:52.931
Import your timetable and set your priorities: your study plan adapts, and knows what you actually did.

00:01:53.966 --> 00:02:00.158
Every morning, you know exactly what to study. And you can find anything with one shortcut, day or night.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:05.397
And you can take it all with you: sheets as PDF, and cards to Anki.

00:02:06.433 --> 00:02:15.417
Language, level of detail, text size, colours: it's all yours to set. And Révise updates itself, never in the middle of a mock exam.

00:02:16.466 --> 00:02:19.935
So, drop in your first course. Révise takes care of the rest.
